# Cloudflare Pages reads this file at deploy time and applies the rules below to
# matching responses. It is config, not a served asset — Pages strips it from the
# published output. Other static hosts ignore it, so the GitHub Pages copy of
# this site simply runs without these headers.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  # Scripts need no 'unsafe-inline': every <script> on the site is a src= to
  # self or cdnjs. Styles do — the pages carry their layout in style="..."
  # attributes, which is exactly what 'unsafe-inline' governs.
  # frame-src is for the embedded Google Map on the home and booking pages;
  # the maps.google.com embed URL redirects to www.google.com, so both are listed.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; frame-src https://maps.google.com https://www.google.com; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; object-src 'none'

# Nothing here is content-hashed — `hero-lumia-logo.jpg` and `main.js` keep
# their names when what is behind them changes. So the browser gets a short
# lease and Cloudflare's edge gets a long one.
#
# The edge lease is a year, and a deploy does NOT purge it. That was assumed
# once and it was wrong: a push went out with new HTML and the edge went on
# serving a main.js from sixteen hours earlier, so the markup asked for a plate
# the stale script had no code to paint and the hero reveal simply did not
# happen — while the same commit was perfectly fine on GitHub Pages, which has
# no edge in front of it. Nothing about the deploy looked wrong.
#
# So the URL is the cache key. /css/* and /js/* are requested with a ?v= that is
# bumped by hand whenever either file changes, which the pages carry and explain
# at the tags themselves; the edge cannot serve a URL it has never seen. Photos
# have no such handle — to force one through, rename the file. To flush the edge
# by hand: Cloudflare > the zone > Caching > Configuration > Custom Purge > URL.
#
# Note the browser lease below is capped by the zone's own Browser Cache TTL
# setting (Caching > Configuration), which currently overrides these max-age
# values to 4 hours. Changing the number here alone will not move it.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, s-maxage=31536000

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=31536000

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=31536000
